BUILD 89 - Travel NPCs answer again (Warden of the Spartan Crypt fix)

- FIXED: the Warden of the Spartan Crypt did nothing when clicked. No dialog box, no
  travel option, nothing. He now opens his menu and takes you down into the crypt,
  which was the only canonical way into that area.
- The same defect affected every traveller you reach by teleporting in: the
  return-to-Helos NPCs in the Soulvizier areas and the enter-offer travellers.
  All 30 travel NPCs are fixed by the same change.
- Cause: an NPC you arrive at by teleport was never woken up, so the game drew him
  but he had no clickable state. Every travel NPC is now woken up before his travel
  offer is presented, using the same method the working Leinth exit portal has always
  used.
- The Helos plaza travellers that already worked keep the exact same routes and
  destinations. No route, no destination and no dialog option changed anywhere.

Quest data only. No database, map or text change: your characters, saves and items
are untouched. Fully quit the game and restart Steam to pick up the update.
